      "hasMoreBelow": false,
      "nextStartLine": null,
      "content": "1|# Blossom Union\n2|\n3|The **Blossom Union** is a fellowship of druid-monks who maintain [[Springarden]], a sacred garden deep within [[Springwood]]. They care for the garden’s ancient trees, flowering paths, holy springs, and fey crossings while protecting pilgrims who come seeking healing, peace, and communion with nature.\n4|\n5|The Union combines druidic stewardship with disciplined martial training. Its members cultivate plants, tend wounded creatures, guide travelers, study fey activity, and defend Springarden from threats. They believe nature is strongest when growth, decay, instinct, and wisdom remain in balance.\n6|\n7|The Union welcomes visitors but expects them to respect the garden. Polluting the pools, harming its creatures, damaging sacred plants, or stealing shrine offerings is considered a serious offense. Those who violate the garden may be barred from Springarden or required to perform a period of service under the Union’s supervision.\n8|\n9|## Springarden’s Keepers\n10|\n11|The Union maintains the garden through several duties:\n12|\n13|- Caring for the sacred pools and their giant flying koi.\n14|- Maintaining paths, bridges, shrines, and flowering groves.\n15|- Treating injured pilgrims, caretakers, and forest creatures.\n16|- Monitoring the boundary between the Material Plane and the Plane of Fey.\n17|- Protecting the garden during Feyfest.\n18|- Investigating creatures or magic that disturb Springarden’s natural calm.\n19|\n20|## Rivalry with the Order of the Emerald Breath\n21|\n22|The [[Blossom Union]] has a long-running rivalry with the [[Order of the Emerald Breath]]. Both factions revere nature, healing, and sacred cultivation, but they disagree sharply over who should control access to [[Springarden]].\n23|\n24|The Order believes Springarden’s sacred plants, healing springs, and fey-touched resources should be studied and shared for the good of communities across [[Stickyickistan]]. The Union considers that attitude dangerously extractive. To them, Springarden is not a public apothecary, research garden, or Arcannabis seed vault. It is a living holy site whose first need is protection.\n25|\n26|The rivalry is usually political and philosophical rather than violent. Union members may refuse Order researchers access to restricted groves, challenge their cultivation methods, or accuse them of dressing ambition up as compassion. In turn, the Order accuses the Union of hoarding blessings while people elsewhere suffer.\n27|\n28|## Notable Members\n29|\n30|- **[[Threeflower]]:** A timid gnome druid who guides visitors and serves as a field representative for the Union.\n31|- **[[Pyrax]]:** A [[Lizardfolk]] fire druid who studies controlled burns and forest renewal.\n32|- **[[Archdruid Xyxl]]:** The Union’s senior spiritual authority and guardian of Springarden’s oldest traditions.",
